      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives is a bit like the difference between a whispering gnome and a sneaky goblin. When you say /z/ as in \"zebra,\" your vocal cords are vibrating, much like a gnome humming a tune. It's a voiced sound, full of life and energy. On the other hand, when you say /s/ as in \"snake,\" your vocal cords stay still, like a goblin hiding in the shadows. It's an unvoiced sound, silent and stealthy. So, the vocal cords are either buzzing with activity or just sitting there, depending on the sound you're making.",
